From ad4c6b194f394a3d0d44137c6837ddf533681cf1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:25:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] livedisplay: adaptive backlight (panel CABC) as a LiveDisplay
 2.0 HAL

LineageOS 17.1 dropped BOARD_HARDWARE_CLASS, so 15.1's lineagehw
AdaptiveBacklight (fix 50) is gone, and its generic sysfs LiveDisplay
service only knows fb0/cabc and fb0/acl. Huawei's lcdkit driver exposes
the BOE NT51017 panel's own CABC as fb0/lcd_cabc_mode (0 off, 1 UI
mode; the kernel re-sends the chosen mode after each panel power-on).

vendor.lineage.livedisplay@2.0-service.ags_w09 implements only
IAdaptiveBacklight on that node and runs in LineageOS's
hal_lineage_livedisplay_sysfs domain, with write access to
sysfs_lcd_cabc. It replaces the stale livedisplay@1.0-service-sdm
package line (that module no longer exists in 17.1).

Tested enforcing: Settings > LiveDisplay > "Reduce power consumption"
flips the panel register both ways and survives screen off/on; 0
denials.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
